  "gaps": [
   "WebGPU only: the projection is WGSL code added by a Babylon MaterialPluginBase to the Standard and PBR materials of the world; a WebGL engine draws the scene without it",
   "a shape drawn by a ShaderMaterial (a textured UnlitMaterial, points, lines, volumes) is not tinted; X_ITE 16.6.0 tints those too",
   "the PBR path (PhysicalMaterial: surfaceAlbedo is tinted before the lights) compiles but was not compared by picture: PhysicalMaterial draws black in the body on this rig with or without a projector, so no tint can show",
   "upVector default: X3DUOM 4.0 says 0 1 0 (used here); X_ITE 16.6.0 reads 0 0 1 for a scene whose version is 4.0 or lower, so a tilted projector with no upVector written is rolled differently there",
   "at most four projectors at a time (X_ITE's maxTextures), the first four that are on; the picture is read nearest-texel, mip levels and TextureProperties filters are not applied (X_ITE's default look is nearest as well)",
   "shadows, shadowColor, shadowIntensity and shadowMapSize are stored and do nothing (X_ITE 16.6.0 does not shadow a projector either)"
